<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Margrethe II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1940</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Margrethe II of Denmark</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Margrethe II was Queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> from 1972 until her abdication on 14 January 2024 in favour of her son, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederik-x">Frederik X</a>. The constitutional change of 1953 allowed her, as eldest daughter of Frederick IX, to inherit the throne. She was the first female monarch of Denmark since <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaret-i-of-denmark">Margaret I</a>, and was also known as an artist, illustrator and costume designer.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/margrethe-ii.jpg" alt="Margrethe II" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes Jansson · CC BY 2.5 dk · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drottning_Margrethe_av_Danmark.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
